    "turns": [
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "Turn the clock back to 1967. What problem was Back-propagation actually trying to solve?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial-hook"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "Back-propagation developed through several strands of adaptive control and neural-network research, with Shunichi Amari's adaptive pattern classifiers and the 1986 Rumelhart-Hinton-Williams paper becoming central references. The method efficiently computes gradients through layered networks.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-learning-representations-by-back-propagating-errors"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.historical-background"
        },
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "That sounds like a promising direction. What mechanism actually makes it work?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "Output error is differentiated backward through the network so each weight receives an update.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-learning-representations-by-back-propagating-errors"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.core-idea"
        },
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "Why did the idea outlive one paper or experiment? What did later researchers actually inherit?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "Experts generally treat back-propagation as the optimization workhorse of neural networks, while acknowledging its multi-decade rediscovery history. Its long-term legacy is making deep layered representations trainable at scale.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-learning-representations-by-back-propagating-errors"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.long-term-legacy"
        },
        {
            "role": "SUMMARY",
            "text": "Back-propagation mattered not only as a result, but as a method that later researchers could test, adapt, and extend.",
